  "provider_query": "Python standard library documentation for the venv module",
  "answer": "Relevant documentation for the Python standard library **`venv`** module:\n\n1. **venv — Creation of virtual environments (Python 3.14)** — Official library reference: creating environments, CLI options, and the `EnvBuilder` API. Added in 3.3; source in `Lib/venv/`.  \n   https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/venv.html\n\n2. **Same page, stable “3” docs** — Current stable library docs for `venv` (creation, isolation, `pyvenv.cfg`, options such as `--system-site-packages`, `--without-pip`, `--upgrade-deps`).  \n   https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html\n\n3. **12. Virtual Environments and Packages (tutorial, 3.13)** — Tutorial on creating, activating, and using virtual environments with `python -m venv`.  \n   https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/venv.html\n\n4. **Tutorial source (CPython)** — RST source for the virtual-environments tutorial (`Doc/tutorial/venv.rst`).  \n   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/HEAD/Doc/tutorial/venv.rst\n\n5. **Development docs tutorial** — Same tutorial on the in-development docs (3.15 alpha).  \n   https://docs.python.org/dev/tutorial/venv.html\n\n6. **pydevtools handbook — venv** — Concise reference: stdlib since 3.3, comparison with virtualenv/uv, flags such as `--upgrade-deps` (3.9+), and that `pyvenv` was removed in 3.8.  \n   https://pydevtools.com/handbook/reference/venv/\n\n7. **Python Land — Python venv** — Practical create/activate/deactivate guide; points to the official docs for full CLI options.  \n   https://python.land/virtual-environments/virtualenv\n\n8. **ZetCode — Python venv** — Short walkthrough of creating and activating environments and of layout (`pyvenv.cfg`, `site-packages`).  \n   https://zetcode.com/python/venv/\n\n**Core usage (from the official docs):** `python -m venv /path/to/env` creates an isolated environment on top of the base interpreter; activate with `source path/bin/activate` (Unix) or `path\\Scripts\\activate` (Windows).",
